{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQpSvCdKTdSepzvWmGX4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Settled: customers choose 2, 3, or 4 equal installments. A remainder from equal splitting goes on the last installment, as planned.\n\nYour answer didn't say how far apart the installments are, so that's the first question.\n\n**Questions**\n\n1. **How far apart are the installments?**\n   - **A. Monthly, with the first due on the invoice's original due date.** For example, 3 installments on a Feb 1 invoice fall on Feb 1, Mar 1 and Apr 1.\n   - **B. Every 2 weeks, starting on the original due date.** The invoice gets paid off faster.\n   - **C. Spread evenly between the original due date and a fixed end date.**\n   - *I recommend A.* Monthly is what customers expect, and 4 installments is a 3-month plan, which stays short.\n\n2. **Which invoices can be split?** This is still open from the last round.\n   - **A. Only `sent` invoices, before their due date.**\n   - **B. Overdue invoices too.** That means deciding what happens to the late fee already added.\n   - *I recommend A.* It leaves the existing overdue and late-fee flow untouched.\n\n3. **What happens when a customer misses an installment?** Today an invoice goes `overdue` when its single due date passes.\n   - **A. The invoice goes `overdue` but only the missed installment is late.** Later installments keep their dates. This is the most forgiving option.\n   - **B. The invoice goes `overdue` and the whole remaining balance is due now.** This is \"acceleration\": the plan is cancelled. It's stricter, and the customer loses the plan after one miss.\n   - **C. A grace period, e.g. 7 days, before A applies.** This adds a rule that doesn't exist today.\n   - *I recommend A.* It keeps the plan useful and makes the smallest change to the status model, since `overdue` still means \"something is late\".\n\n**Held for the next round**\n- **Late fee on a missed installment:** 2% of the missed installment, 2% of the total once, or no fee. This waits on Q3 because acceleration changes what the fee should be based on."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1913,"cache_read_input_tokens":34113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1913},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65cd7f78-dc29-45f0-8059-e2f8f1345fe5","uuid":"28246bf8-1cb9-4da2-a670-6d293a821890","timestamp":"2026-11-26T03:20:22.617Z","request_id":"req_011ChQpSv4gjgBP2fkyxoXVG"}
